    "q-132029": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132029",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}9 & 8 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left of ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero.*",
      "worked_solution": "Let's make entries to the left of ${a}_{44}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}9 & 8 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -4 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+3{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-2){C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 8 & 5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 8 & 5 & -7 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 5 & -7 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 5 & -7 \\\\ -4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-132029-a",
