    "q-132146": {
      "dom_id": "step-q132146",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*",
      "worked_solution": "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -6 & 1 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-2){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-5)\\cdot (-1)^{3+2}|\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10(25+9) \\\\  & =340.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-132146-a",
